---
// The "which metal backup" block. Rendered on a lesson that declares `extra: 'metal'`
// in lessons.js, so nothing is hardcoded to a slug — see src/data/metal.js for why
// this is framed as someone else's test results rather than our own verdict.
import { metalCriteria, metalPicks, metalBands, metalFailed, metalSource, metalVerified,
         metalTests, metalOutcome } from '../data/metal.js';
const band = Object.fromEntries(metalBands.map((b) => [b.key, b.label]));
const badge = { value: 'best value', titanium: 'if you want titanium' };
// Every figure below derives from metalOutcome — see invariant #10. The percentage is
// computed rather than written down, because a typed one silently stops matching the
// counts beside it the first time the source is re-read.
const pctPoor = Math.round((metalOutcome.poor / metalOutcome.reviewed) * 100);
---
<section class="metal">
  <h2 id="choosing-metal">Choosing a metal backup</h2>
  <p class="m-lead">
    “Move it to metal” is easy to say and oddly hard to act on — there are dozens of these things and they
    are not equally good. Here is how to choose one, and a short list that survives.
  </p>

  <div class="callout">
    <span class="label">Whose judgement this is</span>
    <p style="margin:0">
      We rate hardware wallets ourselves, because that judgement is about design and firmware and we can read
      those. <strong>Metal backups are decided by fire, acid and a 20-ton press, and we have not run those
      tests.</strong> <a href={metalSource.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{metalSource.name}</a> has, on
      {' '}{metalOutcome.reviewed} of them — {metalSource.note} <strong>The criteria below are ours; every
      grade and price is his.</strong>
    </p>
  </div>

  <h3>The good news first</h3>
  <p class="m-lead">
    Most of these products are fine. Of the {metalOutcome.reviewed} devices tested, <strong>{metalOutcome.topGrade} came
    through every test with nothing lost</strong>, and only {metalOutcome.poor} — about {pctPoor}% — did badly.
    So this is not a minefield, and you do not need to agonise. You need to avoid a
    <a href="#metal-failures">short list of specific traps</a>, and then pick on the things the stress tests
    don't measure. That second part is what the rest of this section is for.
  </p>
  <ul class="m-tests">
    {metalTests.map((x) => (
      <li><span class="mt-k mono">{x.t}</span><span>{x.d}</span></li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <h3>What actually matters</h3>
  <ol class="m-crit">
    {metalCriteria.map((c) => (
      <li><strong>{c.t}</strong><span>{c.d}</span></li>
    ))}
  </ol>

  <h3>Five that meet all five</h3>
  <p class="m-sub">
    Every one of these scored top marks in all {metalTests.length} of Lopp’s stress tests <em>and</em> meets the
    {' '}{metalCriteria.length} criteria above, which he doesn’t test for. Far more than five would qualify on
    durability alone — this is our shortlist, not a ranking, and deliberately not exhaustive.
  </p>
  <ul class="m-picks">
    {metalPicks.map((p) => (
      <li>
        <span class="m-head">
          <a href={p.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{p.name} ↗</a>
          {p.pick && <span class="m-badge mono">{badge[p.pick]}</span>}
          <span class="m-band mono">{band[p.band]}</span>
        </span>
        <span class="m-method mono">{p.method}</span>
        <span class="m-note">{p.note}</span>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>
  <p class="m-price-note sub">
    Prices are bands rather than figures on purpose. We watch hardware-wallet prices on a schedule and stamp
    them with a date; we don’t watch these, so a precise number would be a promise we couldn’t keep.
  </p>

  <h3 id="metal-failures">The ones to avoid</h3>
  <p class="m-sub">
    The {metalOutcome.poor} that did badly are worth naming, and each failure shows you one of the criteria above
    doing its job.
  </p>
  <ul class="m-failed">
    {metalFailed.map((f) => (
      <li><span class="mf-name">{f.name}</span><span class="mf-why" set:html={f.why}></span></li>
    ))}
  </ul>
  <p class="m-verified mono">Test results checked against the source, and every link above loaded, on {metalVerified}</p>
</section>

<style>
  .metal { margin-top: 2.2rem; }
  .m-lead { color: var(--muted); max-width: 62ch; }
  .m-sub { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.94rem; }

  .m-crit { list-style: none; margin: 1.1rem 0 0; padding: 0; counter-reset: mc;
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.7rem; }
  .m-crit li { counter-increment: mc; display: grid; gap: 0.2rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--line); border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--surface); padding: 0.9rem 1.15rem; }
  .m-crit li strong { color: var(--text); }
  .m-crit li strong::before { content: counter(mc) " · "; color: var(--accent); font-family: var(--mono); }
  .m-crit li span { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.93rem; line-height: 1.55; }

  .m-picks { list-style: none; margin: 1.1rem 0 0; padding: 0;
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.6rem; }
  .m-picks li { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--surface); padding: 0.9rem 1.15rem; display: grid; gap: 0.25rem; }
  .m-head { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: baseline; gap: 0.5rem; }
  .m-head a { font-weight: 650; text-decoration: none; color: var(--accent); }
  .m-head a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .m-badge { font-size: 0.64rem; letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase; font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--accent-ink); background: var(--accent); border-radius: 0.35rem; padding: 0.1rem 0.4rem; }
  .m-band { color: var(--faint); font-size: 0.76rem; margin-left: auto; white-space: nowrap; }
  .m-method { color: var(--safe); font-size: 0.72rem; letter-spacing: 0.03em; }
  .m-note { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; }
  .m-price-note { margin-top: 0.8rem; font-size: 0.86rem; }
  .m-verified { color: var(--faint); font-size: 0.74rem; margin-top: 1rem; }

  /* the three stress tests, stated in his parameters rather than our paraphrase */
  .m-tests { list-style: none; margin: 1rem 0 0; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.45rem; }
  .m-tests li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 5.2rem 1fr; gap: 0.8rem; align-items: baseline;
    font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.55; }
  .m-tests .mt-k { color: var(--accent); font-size: 0.72rem; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  @media (max-width: 560px) { .m-tests li { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.15rem; } }

  /* the failures, each teaching the criterion it broke */
  .m-failed { list-style: none; margin: 1rem 0 0; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.6rem; }
  .m-failed li { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-left: 3px solid var(--warn); border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--surface); padding: 0.85rem 1.1rem; display: grid; gap: 0.2rem; min-width: 0; }
  .m-failed .mf-name { color: var(--text); font-weight: 650; }
  .m-failed .mf-why { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; }
  .m-failed .mf-why a { color: var(--accent); }
</style>
